<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cosipa 1996 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cosipa 1996 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's steel mill Companhia Siderurgica Paulista (Cosipa) issued the following statement on its 1996 results for the holding company.</p>
<p>			  1996			    1995</p>
<p>    Shr loss	  0.57 real	   profit  0.15 real</p>
<p>    Loss		249 million	     profit 64.4 million</p>
<p>    Net revenues    1.242 bln		    1.077 bln</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Brazilian reais.  </p>
<p>NOTE: In a statement, Cosipa said 1996 results were hurt by an increase in financial costs to pay for ongoing investments and an &quot;unfavorable economic-financial scenario,&quot; on which they did not elaborate.</p>
<p>The company said its balance sheet was also hurt by changes in accounting rules, such as not adjusting figures for inflation.</p>
<p>Cosipa also saw a decline in gross margins and non-operational gains.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
